==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|boweman}}, {{m|enm|bouman}}, {{m|enm|boughman}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|bow|man}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbəʊmən/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bowman (ou).wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|bōʹmən}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈboʊmən/}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|bowmen}}

# {{lb|en|archery}} A man who uses a bow; an [[archer]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Jeremiah|4|29}}
#*: The whole city shall flee for the noise of the horsemen and '''bowmen'''.

